_accruals":32.9,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.11326997088851282,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":81.9,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.05016880287347669,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.054392489640126995,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":18.2,"_gate_rev_durability":0.04801201859737314,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":49.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.08567320571423466,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.025316865326497684,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":18.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.011742538064348943,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":80.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.016929999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":11.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"WaFd, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Washington Federal Bank that provides lending, depository, insurance, and other banking services in the United States. The company provides deposit products, including business and personal checking accounts, and term certificates of deposit, as well as money market accounts and passbook savings accounts. It offers single-family residential, construction, land acquisition and development, consumer lot, multi-family residential, commercial real estate, home equity, business, and consumer loans, as well as commercial and industrial loans. In addition, the company offers insurance brokerage services, such as individual and business insurance policies; holds and markets real estate properties; and debit and credit cards, as well as acts as the trustee. Additionally, it provides technology and data services; and personalized financial guidance and investment services. It serves consumers, mid-sized and large businesses, and owners and developers of commercial real estate. The company was formerly known as Washington Federal, Inc. and changed its name to WaFd, Inc. in September 2023. WaFd, Inc. was founded in 1917 and is headquartered in Seattle, Washington.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brent J. Beardall CPA | President, CEO & Vice Chairman | Age 54 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $360K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $103K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["WaFd, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $2.2B market cap on $725M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 11-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $208M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.05\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 8.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 56% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"WaFd, Inc. (NASDAQ:WAFD) Plans Quarterly Dividend of $0.27","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/wafd-inc-nasdaqwafd-plans-quarterly-dividend-of-0-27.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794411057.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Head-To-Head Review: WaFd (WAFD) and Its Competitors","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/head-to-head-review-wafd-wafd-and-its-competitors.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794402909.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.586,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Zacks Research Issues Pessimistic Outlook for WaFd Earnings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/zacks-research-issues-pessimistic-outlook-for-wafd-earnings.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794381182.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance","legal"]},{"title":"WaFd declares $0.27 dividend (NASDAQ:WAFD)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4670421-wafd-declares-0_27-dividend","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794374182.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"WaFd (NASDAQ:WAFD) Issues Quarterly Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/16/wafd-nasdaqwafd-issues-quarterly-earnings-results.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794348378.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"